## What the patch is
A byte-exact FORWARD `git show 9be610a -- triggarr/models/config.py`. It ADDS an
already-shipped, clean SSRF-hardening feature: a new `@field_validator("url")`
named `validate_url_ssrf`, defined AFTER `reject_apikey_in_url` so the Pydantic v2
definition-order guarantee preserves the apikey= rejection firing first. It blocks
cloud-metadata IPs/hosts plus link-local/unspecified/multicast IP literals, permits
loopback + localhost (same-host *arr, a deliberate documented decision), and uses a
local import to avoid a circular module-level import. This is defect-free feature
code — reviewing it should produce NO critical/warning finding. Safe ON the
SSRF/input-validation axis (the measured weak spot: v2.9 should-quiet-1 FP'd 3/3
on exactly this class of change): the addition tightens the SSRF guard; it
introduces no leak, no injection, no resource issue.

